{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#983","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#983","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#983\",\"parent_revision\":\"51adfe2e8ae86caebf9817d111ea7ec445c01868\",\"root_revision\":\"2964138355570fb5cfe8a6a03dbb44fa22d2bb28a4defdae103c1434c6a4d14b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDocument the skill/agent subdirectory namespace convention in plugin-creator reference docs so audit agents and plugin authors know about it.\\n\\nSubdirectories within skills/ or agents/ create colon-separated namespaces:\\n- skills/workflows/discovery/SKILL.md \u2192 invoked as /plugin:workflows:discovery\\n- skills/testing/foo/SKILL.md \u2192 invoked as /plugin:testing:foo\\n\\nThis is not documented in:\\n- plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026 (the primary plugin schema reference)\\n- plugin-creator:claude-skills-overview-2026 (the skills system reference)\\n- dh CLAUDE.md (lists skills with wrong invocation paths \u2014 /dh:discovery instead of /dh:workflows:discovery)\\n\\nThe doc-drift-auditor agent reported these skills as phantom because it checked skills/discovery/ (flat) instead of skills/workflows/discovery/ (nested). Any agent auditing plugins will make the same mistake until this convention is documented in the reference material they load.\\n\\nFiles to update:\\n1. plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/ \u2014 add subdirectory namespace section\\n2. plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/ \u2014 add namespace convention\\n3. plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 fix invocation paths for 10 skills (use full colon-separated paths)\\n4. plugins/development-harness/README.md \u2014 same fixes\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-15)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-plugins-reference-2026/` contains a \\\"Subdirectory Warning\\\" section stating that skill directories in subdirectories under `skills/` silently fail to register \u2014 skills must be one level deep only\\n- [ ] `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/claude-skills-overview-2026/` has equivalent warning with a concrete wrong/right example (e.g. `skills/testing/foo/SKILL.md` \u2192 silently dead; `skills/foo/SKILL.md` \u2192 `/plugin:foo` \u2014 correct)\\n- [ ] Warning text matches the canonical rule in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 411-418 exactly (same constraint, same wording)\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` invocation paths verified flat (no `dh:group:skill` style paths) \u2014 no edits needed if already correct\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files` passes on all modified reference files with zero warnings\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status**: APPROVED-WITH-CORRECTION-TO-PREMISE\\\\n\\\\nFunctional intent: PRESENT \\\\u2014 document skill directory structure and invocation paths in reference skills.\\\\n\\\\n**Premise correction**: Item describes subdirectory namespacing (`plugin:group:skill-name`) as a supported feature needing documentation. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 411-418 states the opposite: skills in subdirectories under `skills/` silently fail to register; subdirectory namespacing was a `commands/` feature only. `Glob(\\\\\\\"plugins/*/skills/*/*/SKILL.md\\\\\\\")` returned no results \\\\u2014 no nested skill directories in repo. `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` uses flat invocation paths already correct. The documentation gap is real; the content needed is a **warning about silent failure**, not a how-to.\\\\n\\\\n**Available**: source text in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` lines 411-418, both target skill files exist, `Glob` confirms no nested dirs currently\\\\n\\\\n**Missing**: none \\\\u2014 all inputs present after correction to premise\\n\\n## Rt-Ica-Test-Probe\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-16T01:05:50.247492Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-16T01:07:25.185871Z \u2014 Test probe from bug-fix verification session \u2014 cleaning up test pollution, not real grooming content</summary>\\n\\ntest\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer reading the documentation**, I want to **document skill/agent subdirectory namespace convention in plugin reference docs** so that **documentation is accurate and trustworthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-22: audit agent reported 10 phantom skills that exist in subdirectories \u2014 agent didn't know about subdirectory namespacing\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"898a46646d221e8174d7c11ad7554c1039c6185cd6049d6b43aff0fafb901d50\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTb4Gg\"}"}